  wModel: { title: 'the application, in four parts', lines: [
    '**APPLICATION · the post of operations manager · N. Barakat · 3 June**',
    '**I am applying for the post of operations manager, advertised on 28 May.** **I have been traffic and depot manager here for four years and I am not going to spend a paragraph on my interest in the company; you have a vacancy and this paper is about it.**',
    '**WHAT I HAVE DONE, WITH THE BASIS OF EVERY FIGURE.** **Waste fell from 11.2 per cent to 8.4 over the nine months to April — spoilage and rework as a share of raw input by weight, from the line sheets, which are the figures the owners see and not the kinder ones.** **Vehicle availability rose by about six percentage points, measured after I stopped counting a repairable vehicle as available, so the real movement is larger than the figure.** **And the yield trend nobody had reported for four months was found because I put a four-period figure beside every measure, which is worth about 400,000 a year and is the piece of work I am proudest of, because it was invisible.**',
    '**WHAT I HAVE NOT DONE, AND YOU WOULD FIND THESE OUT ANYWAY.** **I have never run a payroll and I have never managed more than fourteen people; this post has thirty-one.** **I have no experience of a unit that was losing money, and I do not know whether I would be good at it.** **I left the drivers’ training for two years, which is why we have one man who can take a load to the border, and that is a failure of mine and not of his.**',
    '**WHAT I WOULD DO IN THE FIRST NINETY DAYS, WHICH IS ONE QUESTION AND NOT A PROGRAMME.** **I do not know whether the Latakia depot is profitable on its own, and neither does anybody else, because its costs are carried in the Homs accounts.** **In the first month I would find out — a basis, a period, a source and an answer in writing.** **Every other decision about the coast depends on it, and I am not going to propose a plan for a depot whose own numbers nobody has.** **I would not change the rota, the tariff or the depot structure before that answer.**',
    '**THE STRONGEST ARGUMENT AGAINST APPOINTING ME, AND I DO NOT DISMISS IT.** **I have never run a loss-making unit, and this one may become one if the coast trade does not recover.** **A manager who has only ever improved a healthy operation has not been tested on the decisions that actually cost people their jobs.** **I would answer it this way: if the Latakia answer is bad, I would put the closure case in front of you within the first ninety days rather than spend a year improving something that should not exist — and I would rather say that now than discover in March that I could not.**',
    '**AND THE LAST THING, WHICH IS WHAT I THINK YOU ARE ACTUALLY DECIDING.** **Not whether I am impressive on two pages.** **Whether, on the day a load is impounded at the border or a customer finds a fault before we do, I am the person you would rather have in the building.** **On that, the only evidence I can offer is four years of what I did when something went wrong, which is in the files and in the people who worked for me, and both are available to you without my help.**' ] },
